        "blast_url": "https://blast.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/Blast.cgi?PAGE_TYPE=BlastSearch&PROG_DEF=blastn&BLAST_SPEC=GDH_GCA_965601635.2",
        "comments": "The assembly daBelPere1.hap1.2 is based on 24x PacBio data and Arima2 Hi-C data generated by the Darwin Tree of Life Project\n(https://www.darwintreeoflife.org/). The assembly process included the following sequence of steps: initial PacBio assembly generation with Hifiasm in Hi-C integrated assembly mode, and Hi-C based scaffolding with YaHS. The mitochondrial and plastid genomes were assembled using OATK. Finally, each haplotype assembly was analysed and manually improved using TreeVal. Chromosome-scale scaffolds confirmed by the Hi-C data have been named in order of size. We can see on the HiC map that the two haplotypes are highly divergent compared to each other for some of the chromosomes. The most divergente one is Chromosome 5. HiC signal is poor for some of the hap2 chromosomes, what made it difficult to curate both haplotypes.",
